ch as the name of a page of hypertext, often with the file name extension .html or .htm.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="125493">web address</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1520348">ୱେବ୍ ଠିକଣା</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14889_87410_484605"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An object that supports the OLE protocol for object linking and embedding.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="87410">OLE object</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="484605">OLE ଅବଜେକ୍ଟ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14895_397169_1957557"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A third-party hardware device or product that connects a legacy PBX to a LAN. An IP/VoIP gateway translates or converts TDM or telephony circuit-switched protocols to packet switched protocols that can be used on a VoIP-based network.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="397169">IP/VoIP gateway</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1957557">IP/VoIP ଗେଟୱେ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14897_231964_485210"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In statistical or scientific data, a bar that shows the potential error or degree of uncertainty relative to each data marker in a series.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="231964">error bar</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="485210">ତ୍ରୁଟି ଦଣ୍ଡିକା</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14901_152051_485014"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The points where playback of a file or clip begins and ends. There are two trim points: start trim point and end trim point.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="152051">trim points</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="485014">କର୍ତ୍ତନ ବିନ୍ଦୁ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14905_318357_485711"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The &gt; character.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="318357">greater than sign</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang