ed folder mailbox policy is applied to a user’s mailbox, all the managed folders that are linked to the policy are deployed in a single operation, thereby making the deployment of messaging records management (MRM) easier.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2161198">UM mailbox policy</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1957595">ପରିଚାଳିତ ଫୋଲ୍ଡର୍ ମେଲବାକ୍ସ ପଲିସୀ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15_397203_1957595"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A logical grouping of managed folders. When a managed folder mailbox policy is applied to a user’s mailbox, all the managed folders that are linked to the policy are deployed in a single operation, thereby making the deployment of messaging records management (MRM) easier.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="397203">managed folder mailbox policy</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1957595">ପରିଚାଳିତ ଫୋଲ୍ଡର୍ ମେଲବାକ୍ସ ପଲିସୀ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1500_7883_1259823"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Pertaining to an entity such as the device, program, file, record or portion of the screen that is currently operational or subject to command operations.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="788