 type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19213_652185_1881406"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Microsoft Office Web Component that provides the interactive functionality of a spreadsheet on a Web page. You can enter data, add formulas and functions, apply filters, change formatting, and recalculate.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="652185">Spreadsheet Component</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1881406">ସ୍ପ୍ରେଡ୍‌ସିଟ୍ ଉପାଦାନ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19215_652187_1259213"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The default text font for worksheets. The standard font determines the default font for the Normal cell style.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="652187">standard font</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259213">ମାନାଙ୍କ ପଣ୍ଟ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19219_652191_1426220"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A date that you set [rather than the current date] for reporting the time, cost, or performance condition of a project.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="652191">status date</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1426220">ଷ୍ଟାଟସ୍ ତାରିଖ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19221_652193_1259214"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A description of the status of a member's project work and related work.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="652193">status report</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259214">ଅବସ୍ଥିତି ରିପୋର୍ଟ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19229_652201_1426221"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A task that is made up of subtasks and summarizes those subtasks. Use outlining to create summary tasks. Project automatically determines summary task information [such as duration and cost] by using information from the subtasks.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="652201">summary task</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1426221">ସାରାଂଶ ଟାସ୍କ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19232_652204_1426222"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An horizontal or vertical line that divides a diagram into partitions and which is used to arrange related parts of a process.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="652204">swimlane</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1426222">ସୁଇମଲେନ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19234_652206_1802619"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Any application or process that you want to model. Examples of systems include a computer game, a process for assembling microchips, and a library information system.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="652206">system</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1802619">ସିଷ୍ଟମ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19250_652222_1881407"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">One of a set of major and minor fonts that is applied to a file. Theme fonts, theme colors, and theme effects compose a theme.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="652222">theme font</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1881407">ଥିମ୍ ଫଣ୍ଟ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19251_652223_1881408"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of pane that presents the current scanned document as one or more small images.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="652223">thumbnail pane</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1881408">ଥମ୍ଵନେଲ୍ ଫଳକ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19254_652226_1426223"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The time period indicator at the top of the Gantt views, the Resource Graph view, the Task Usage view, and the Resource Usage view. You can customize it to show up to three tiers that can display various time units: top, middle, and bottom.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="652226">timescale</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1426223">ସମୟସ୍କେଲ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19258_652230_1881409"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A special row in a list or table that provides a selection of aggregate functions useful for working with numerical data.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="652230">total row</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1881409">ସର୍ବମୋଟ ଧାଡି</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19258_760167_1881409"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A special row in a list or table that provides a selection of aggregate functions useful for working with numerical data.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="760167">totals row</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1881409">ସର୍ବମୋଟ ଧାଡି</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19261_652233_1881410"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An arrow that shows the relationship between the active cell and its related cells. Tracer arrows are blue when pointing from a cell that provides data to another cell, and red if a cell contains an error value, such as #DIV/0!.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="652233">tracer arrow</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1881410">ଟ୍ରେସର୍ ତୀର</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19264_652236_1881411"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Optional text for a trendline, including either the regression equation or the R-squared value, or both. A trendline label can be formatted and moved; it cannot be sized.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="652236">trendline label</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1881411">ଟ୍ରେଣ୍ଡଲାଇନ୍ ଲେବଲ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19265_652237_1259215"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A folder or file path on your computer or a location on your intranet from which it is safe to run code. Default trusted locations include the Templates, Addins, and Startup folders, and you can specify your own trusted locations.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="652237">trusted location</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259215">ବିଶ୍ୱସ୍ଥ ଅବସ୍ଥାନ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19266_652238_1881412"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A list of software publisher certificates used to digitally sign code, such as macros. Because you explicitly trust the software publishers, their code is allowed to run on your computer without needing to prompt for permission.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="652238">trusted publisher store</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1881412">ବିଶ୍ଵସ୍ତ ପ୍ରକାଶକ ଷ୍ଟୋର୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19271_652243_1426224"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The percentage of a work resource’s time that is assigned to a task.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="652243">unit</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1426224">ଏକକଗୁଡ଼ିକ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19273_652245_1881413"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In line charts with multiple data series, bars that indicate the difference between data points in the first and last series.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="652245">up-down bars</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1881413">ଉପର-ତଳ ଦଣ୍ଡିକା</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19276_652248_1881414"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A chart axis that displays scaled numerical values.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="652248">value axis</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1881414">ମୂଲ୍ୟ ଅକ୍ଷ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1928_90900_1259828"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To break input into smaller chunks so that a program can act upon the information.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="90900">parse</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259828">ବିଶ୍ଳେଷଣ କରିବା</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1928_90900_484627"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To break input into smaller chunks so that a program can act upon the information.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="90900">parse</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="484627">ପାର୍ସ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19280_652252_1259216"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A bar displayed along the left side of a document window. You can use the vertical ruler to adjust the top and bottom page margins and the row height in tables.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="652252">vertical ruler</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259216">ଅନୁଲମ୍ବ ରୁଲର୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19285_652286_1259217"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A calendar in widespread use. It was introduced in 1582 A.D. as a revision to the Julian calendar.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="652286">Gregorian calendar</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259217">ଗ୍ରେଗୋରିଆନ୍ କ୍ୟାଲେଣ୍ଡର୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19291_652263_1259218"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An XML structure that consists of a start tag, an end tag, and the information between the tags. Elements can have attributes and can contain other elements.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="652263">XML element</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259218">XML ଉପାଦାନ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19295_652267_1881415"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A switch (\#) or instruction that specifies how Microsoft Word will display the numeric result of a field.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="652267">numeric picture switch</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1881415">ସଂଖ୍ୟାକୃତ ଛବି ସୁଇଚ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19296_652268_1881416"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A switch (\*) or instruction that specifies the capitalization, numeral style, and character formatting that Microsoft Word uses in a field result.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="652268">format switch</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><t