, any one of the views. Every tab contains functionally related commands and other controls that are organized in groups. Typically, ribbon tabs are labeled.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1309629">ribbon tab</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1881600">ରିବନ୍ ଟ୍ୟାବ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1975_73133_1259830"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A designation used to conduct sorting or searching operations.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="73133">keyword</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259830">କିଓ୍ୱାର୍ଡ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19767_674770_2768388"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A rating unit, e.g. assigning a "one-star rating" to an image.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="674770">star</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2768388">ତାରକା</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1978_45320_1259831"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To enter numbers on a device, such as telephone or mobile, in order to make a phone call.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="45320">dial</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259831">ଡାୟଲ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19780_2466458_2470776"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The audio effect ​that creates the perception that there are many more sources of sound then are currently present. This is a well-known and industry term for the technique of creating a surround sound experience for users listening to audio with regular stereo headphones.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2466458">virtual surround sound</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2470776">ଭର୍ଚ୍ୟୁଆଲ୍‌ ସରାଉଣ୍ଡ ସାଉଣ୍ଡ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19780_682693_2470776"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The audio effect ​that creates the perception that there are many more sources of sound then are currently present. This is a well-known and industry term for the technique of creating a surround sound experience for users listening to audio with regular stereo headphones.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="682693">virtual surround</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2470776">ଭର୍ଚ୍ୟୁଆଲ୍‌ ସରାଉଣ୍ଡ ସାଉଣ୍ଡ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1979_63495_1259832"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A graphic symbol used on the user interface to assist with navigation.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="63495">icon</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259832">ଚିତ୍ରସଙ୍କେତ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1979_63495_484434"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A graphic symbol used on the user interface to assist with navigation.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="63495">icon</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="484434">ଆଇକନ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19792_685384_1881424"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An effect that applies to the exterior border around each character of your text or shape.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="685384">outline effect</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1881424">ବାହ୍ୟରେଖା ପ୍ରଭାବ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19793_685388_1259228"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An effect that applies to the appearance of the interior of an enclosed text character or other shape.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="685388">fill effect</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259228">ପରିପୂର୍ଣ୍ଣ ପ୍ରଭାବ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="198_112365_484730"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Any combination of keys that must be pressed simultaneously.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="112365">shortcut key</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="484730">ସର୍ଟକଟ୍ କୀ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="198_112365_485689"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Any combination of keys that must be pressed simultaneously.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="112365">shortcut key</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="485689">କୀ ସମ୍ମେଳନ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="198_318149_484730"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Any combination of keys that must be pressed simultaneously.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="318149">key combination</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="484730">ସର୍ଟକଟ୍ କୀ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="198_318149_485689"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Any combination of keys that must be pressed simultaneously.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="318149">key combination</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="485689">କୀ ସମ୍ମେଳନ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19800_685897_1259229"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A file that contains the data that a program will process and store in a destination file.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="685897">source file</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259229">ଉତ୍ସ ଫାଇଲ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19806_2908028_1957439"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of resource record in the Domain Name System that associates a computer's true (canonical) name with any alias names also used by the computer. Some domain registrars use CNAME records to redirect or redelegate domain names.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2908028">CNAME</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1957439">CNAME ରେକର୍ଡ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19806_686253_1957439"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of resource record in the Domain Name System that associates a computer's true (canonical) name with any alias names also used by the computer. Some domain registrars use CNAME records to redirect or redelegate domain names.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="686253">canonical name record</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1957439">CNAME ରେକର୍ଡ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19806_686254_1957439"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of resource record in the Domain Name System that associates a computer's true (canonical) name with any alias names also used by the computer. Some domain registrars use CNAME records to redirect or redelegate domain names.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="686254">CNAME record</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1957439">CNAME ରେକର୍ଡ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19810_686305_1957493"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The owner of the customer relationship with customers who buy second-level domains. There may be many registrars for a single top-level domain. Registrars maintain detailed customer information in their databases, such as the customer's contact address, telephone number, and email address. Customers usually manage their second-level domains at the registrar's Web site, and the registrar updates the registry database when necessary (for example, when a customer renews a domain name).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="686305">domain name registrar</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1957493">ଡୋମେନ୍ ନାମ ପ୍ରବନ୍ଧକ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19828_686821_1957627"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of resource record in the Domain Name System (DNS) specifying how Internet email should be routed using the Simple Mail Transfer Protocol (SMTP). Each MX record contains a preference and a host name, so that the collection of MX records for a given domain name point to the servers that should receive email for that domain, and their priority relative to each other.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="686821">mail exchange record</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1957627">MX ରେକର୍ଡ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19828_686822_1957627"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of resource record in the Domain Name System (DNS) specifying how Internet email should be routed using the Simple Mail Transfer Protocol (SMTP). Each MX record contains a preference and a host name, so that the collection of MX records for a given domain name point to the servers that should receive email for that domain, and their priority relative to each other.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="686822">MX record</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1957627">MX ରେକର୍ଡ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19838_687152_1881426"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The distance between the camera’s lens and the image plane.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="687152">focal length</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1881426">ଫୋକାଲ୍ ଲମ୍ଵା</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1989_48436_484338"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An area of storage that is formatted with a file system and has an identifier to access it.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="48436">drive</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="484338">ଡ୍ରାଇଭ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1992_108620_484714"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A program that searches for key words in documents, databases, Internet content or other files.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="108620">search engine</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="484714">ସନ୍ଧାନକାରୀ ଇଞ୍ଜିନ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19941_690680_2767890"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To grant a person or entity the right to use a software product, as described in the terms of the license agreement.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="690680">license</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2767890">ଲାଇସେନ୍ସ କରିବା</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="19945_690967_1951428"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that identifies elements in your file that aren't supported or will behave differently in a different format or previous version of the product.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="690967">Compatibility Checker</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1951428">ସୁସଙ୍ଗତ ଚେକର୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1999_1359036_1259000"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A list of entities such as people, groups, or organizations with whom users communicate.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1359036">Contacts list</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259000">ସମ୍ପର୍କ ତାଲିକା</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1999_184612_1259000"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A list of entities such as people, groups, or organizations with whom users communicate.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="184612">contact list</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259000">ସମ୍ପର୍କ ତାଲିକା</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1999_763863_1259000"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A list of entities such as people, groups, or organizations with whom users communicate.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="763863">buddy list</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><te