w that shows all of the resources on a project and their work over time. This makes it easy to rearrange work, schedule new work, and manage a team's load.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1054764">Team Planner</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1426240">ଟିମ୍ ପ୍ଲାନର୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22735_1054767_1259389"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that allows the application of tags to individual Outlook items to specify retention policy for that message, conversation or other item.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1054767">Retention Policy</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259389">ରିଟେନସନ୍ ପଲିସି</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22771_1054905_1957780"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A user interface implemented by a software application via a component of a web server, such as IIS.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1054905">web portal</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1957780">ୱେବ୍ ପୋର୍ଟାଲ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22781_1054938_1519775"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To permit someone else to perform an action.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1054938">allow</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1519775">ଅନୁମତି ଦେବା</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2279_26594_1259837"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A piece of software that functions as an electronic calendar used for scheduling.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="26594">calendar program</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259837">କ୍ୟାଲେଣ୍ଡର୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2279_26594_484145"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A piece of software that functions as an electronic calendar used for scheduling.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="26594">calendar program</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="484145">କ୍ଯାଲେଣ୍ଡର୍ ପ୍ରୋଗ୍ରାମ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2279_294450_1259837"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A piece of software that functions as an electronic calendar used for scheduling.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="294450">calendar</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259837">କ୍ୟାଲେଣ୍ଡର୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2279_294450_484145"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A piece of software that functions as an electronic calendar used for scheduling.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="294450">calendar</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="484145">କ୍ଯାଲେଣ୍ଡର୍ ପ୍ରୋଗ୍ରାମ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22798_1055051_2701029"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A microprocessor architecture developed in 1992 by Motorola and IBM, with some participation by Apple. A PowerPC microprocessor is RISC-based and superscalar, with a 64-bit data bus and 32-bit address bus. It also has separate data and instruction caches, although the size of each varies by implementation. All PowerPC microprocessors have multiple integer and floating-point units. The voltage and operating speed varies with the implementation. Starting with the PowerPC 740, the microprocessors were manufactured with copper, instead of aluminum, for better performance and reliability.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1055051">PowerPC</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2701029">PowerPC</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22823_1055132_1259390"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The navigation button used to return to recently visited Web pages in Internet Explorer, Microsoft Edge, and other internet browsers.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1055132">Back</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259390">ପଛ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22826_1055147_1957452"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A staging area that contains representations of selected objects and attributes in a connected data source.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1055147">connector space</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1957452">କନେକ୍ଟର୍ ଖାଲି ସ୍ଥାନ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22828_1055149_1957603"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The data store that is used by ILM to contain the aggregated identity information from multiple connected data sources, providing a single global, integrated view of all combined objects.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1055149">metaverse</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1957603">ମେଟାଭର୍ସ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2285_109836_1881104"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A join in which records from a table are combined with other records from the same table when there are matching values in the joined fields. A self-join can be an inner join or an outer join. In database diagrams, a self-join is called a reflexive relationship.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="109836">self-join</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1881104">ନିଜେ-ଯୋଗଦାନ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22865_1055946_1259391"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Information that describes the current location of a computer. The location is entered manually in Default Location, and can be used by programs to determine the location of a computer when a location sensor is unavailable.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1055946">default location</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259391">ଡିଫଲ୍ଟ ଅବସ୍ଥାନ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22886_1056046_1957742"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A software system that retrieves information from a source data store and synchronizes (pushes) to a target data store. Examples of synchronization engines are the ILM 2007 and FIM 2010 synchronization engines, and the service that synchronizes data rows in the SQL Server Express database with objects in the Microsoft Office Outlook data store.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1056046">synchronization engine</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1957742">ସିଂକ୍ରୋନାଇଜେସନ୍ ଇଞ୍ଜିନ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22886_1056047_1957742"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A software system that retrieves information from a source data store and synchronizes (pushes) to a target data store. Examples of synchronization engines are the ILM 2007 and FIM 2010 synchronization engines, and the service that synchronizes data rows in the SQL Server Express database with objects in the Microsoft Office Outlook data store.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1056047">SyncEngine</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1957742">ସିଂକ୍ରୋନାଇଜେସନ୍ ଇଞ୍ଜିନ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22889_1056052_1959902"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To refuse to accept a file or message.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1056052">reject</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1959902">ପ୍ରତ୍ୟାକ୍ଷାନ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2290_103825_1259838"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Generally, any part of a computer system or network, such as a disk drive, printer, or memory, that can be allotted to a running program or a process.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="103825">resource</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259838">ସମ୍ବଳ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22904_1056071_1957428"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of components and services that enable users to access their Exchange mailboxes through the Outlook Web Access application.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1056071">Client Access server</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1957428">କ୍ଲାଏଣ୍ଟ୍ ଆକ୍ସେସ୍ ସର୍ଭର୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2291_184207_1881232"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The hierarchical HTML tag structure of an opened HTML document that appears in a task pane window.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="184207">tag tree</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1881232">ଟ୍ୟାଗ୍ ଟ୍ରୀ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22911_1056204_1259392"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A term that can be added to a search to filter the results by a specific property (for example, by author). Relevant search filters appear under the search box in any open folder.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1056204">search filter</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259392">ସନ୍ଧାନ ଫିଲ୍ଟର</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22919_1056243_1957382"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A collection of Internet Protocol subnets, usually used to connect a group of computers that are physically close to each other.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1056243">Active Directory site</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1957382">Active Directory ସାଇଟ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22926_1056255_1957379"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of sign-in credentials (username and password) for an Active Directory account.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1056255">Active Directory credentials</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1957379">Active Directory କ୍ରେଡେନସିଆଲ୍ ଗୁଡିକ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22928_1056257_1957376"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The identity of a user, which can be used to grant access to resources or authority to perform certain tasks.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1056257">Active Directory account</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1957376">Active Directory ଏକାଉଣ୍ଟ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2293_79701_484554"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A rectangular bar displayed in an application's window, often at the top, from which menus can be selected by the user.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="79701">menu bar</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="484554">ମେନୁ ଦଣ୍ଡିକା</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22931_1056336_1259393"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of corruption that affects the data in the Windows heap, such as damages caused by a buffer overrun, writing to a stray pointer or a double-free.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1056336">heap corruption</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259393">ବହୁସଂଖ୍ୟକ ତ୍ରୁଟି</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22944_1056351_1259394"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A soft keyboard that is displayed with a different set of settings by default (larger buttons, bigger size, etc.) when you launch the Tablet PC Input Panel with touch. This is to facilitate touch input.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1056351">touch keyboard</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259394">ସ୍ପର୍ଶ କିବୋର୍ଡ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22951_1056450_1259395"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A two-way device provided by a cable provider that enables some one-way digital CableCARD-based consumer electronic devices such as high-definition DVRs and Media Center PCs to access digital cable channels delivered using switched digital video.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1056450">tuning adapter</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259395">TA</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22951_1056452_1259395"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A two-way device provided by a cable provider that enables some one-way digital CableCARD-based consumer electronic devices such as high-definition DVRs and Media Center PCs to access digital cable channels delivered using switched digital video.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1056452">TA</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259395">TA</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22975_1056711_1995019"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A small, affordable laptop that is designed to perform a limited number of tasks such as web browsing and email.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1056711">netbook</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1995019">ନେଟ୍‌ବୁକ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22975_1099729_1995019"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A small, affordable laptop that is designed to perform a limited number of tasks such as web browsing and email.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1099729">small notebook PC</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1995019">ନେଟ୍‌ବୁକ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2299_232415_485224"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A message that appears at a specified interval before an appointment, meeting, or task that announces when the activity is set to occur.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="232415">reminder</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="485224">ସ୍ମାରକ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22992_1056886_1259396"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A real-time, physical action applied to an object, in which multiple contact points are used simultaneously.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1056886">multitouch</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259396">ଏକାଧିକ-ସ୍ପର୍ଶ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="22992_1056887_1259396"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A real-time, physical action applied to an object, in which multiple contact points are used simultaneously.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1056887">multi-touch</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259396">ଏକାଧିକ-ସ୍ପର୍ଶ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2301_314116_1259839"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An amount that is the difference between the sum of debit entries and the sum of credit entries entered into an account during a financial period.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="314116">account balance</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259839">ଆକାଉଣ୍ଟ୍ ଭାରସାମ୍ୟ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2301_616949_1259839"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An amount that is the difference between the sum of debit entries and the sum of credit entries entered into an account during a financial period.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="616949">balance</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259839">ଆକାଉଣ୍ଟ୍ ଭାରସାମ୍ୟ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="23043_1057319_1259397"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A device used to write CD-ROMs. Because a disc can be written only once on these machines, they are used most commonly to create CD-ROMs for data archives or to produce CD-ROM masters that can be duplicated for mass distribution.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1057319">CD recorder</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259397">CD ବର୍ଣ୍ଣର୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="23043_1057320_1259397"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A device used to write CD-ROMs. Because a disc can be written only once on these machines, they are used most commonly to create CD-ROMs for data archives or to produce CD-ROM masters that can be duplicated for mass distribution.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1057320">CD burner</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259397">CD ବର୍ଣ୍ଣର୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2306_210486_1881250"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The formal name for Word 12 file format. This format has an open, royalty-free specification, and is the technology licensed to external parties. This license is the subject in the messaging points where “Open, royalty-free license” is discussed.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="210486">Word XML Format</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1881250">Word XML ଫର୍ମାଟ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="23092_1058116_1259398"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that ensures that all components of a file are preserved, even if they are supported only by the rich client and not viewable in Web Companions.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1058116">Document Integrity</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259398">ଡକ୍ୟୁମେଣ୍ଟ ଅଖଣ୍ଡତା</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2314_117926_1259006"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To change between states or modes.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="117926">switch</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259006">ସୁଇଚ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2316_138366_2736508"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A format that can be applied to selected text characters.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="138366">character formatting</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2736508">ବର୍ଣ୍ଣ ଫର୍ମାଟିଂ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="23174_1060963_1519887"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The heading for information about the time at which something was added, changed, or re-posted.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1060963">updated</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1519887">ଅଦ୍ୟତିତ ହୋଇଛି</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="23177_1060970_1374331"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A customizable page that launches with Windows Live Messenger and features a summary of news and weather, allows a customer to preview their Windows Live Mail inbox and search the Internet.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1060970">Today page</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1374331">ଆଜିର ପୃଷ୍ଠା</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="23178_1060971_1519875"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The title of the window in which the Windows Live Messenger Today page is displayed.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1060971">Today</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1519875">ଆଜି</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="23180_1060974_1881522"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A text box where someone enters the email addresses of the primary recipients of an email message.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1060974">To box</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1881522">ପ୍ରାପ୍ତେଷୁ ବାକ୍ସ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="23184_1060982_1259399"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of features that enables users to improve the quality of their images with just one or two clicks. Galleries help the user optimize characteristics such as brightness, contrast, color, and sharpness.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1060982">Corrections</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259399">ସଂଶୋଧନ ସମୂହ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="23200_1062908_1259400"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that enables Tablet PC users to convert an ink drawing to a standard OfficeArt shape, which can be formatted with colors and effects exactly as if it were inserted using “Insert Shape.”</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1062908">Convert to Shape</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259400">ଆକାରକୁ ରୂପାନ୍ତରିତ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="23201_1062909_1259401"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that enables presenters to capture all the elements of a live presentation, including narration, slides, mouse clicks, A/V playback, and laser pointer highlights. The user can select which presentation aspects to record.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1062909">Record Slide Show</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259401">ଲିପିବଦ୍ଧ ସ୍ଲାଇଡ୍ ସୋ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="23214_1064085_1650294"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A map view created from aerial photos that shows buildings, roads, and geographical features.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1064085">aerial view</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1650294">ଏରିଏଲ୍ ଭ୍ୟୁ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2323_61200_3041982"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Pertaining to the base-16 number system represented by the digits 0 through 9 and the uppercase or lowercase letters A (equivalent to decimal 10) through F (equivalent to decimal 15). Hexadecimal values are commonly used in HTML code to identify colors.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="61200">hex</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3041982">ହେକ୍ସ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2323_61201_3041982"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Pertaining to the base-16 number system represented by the digits 0 through 9 and the uppercase or lowercase letters A (equivalent to decimal 10) through F (equivalent to decimal 15). Hexadecimal values are commonly used in HTML code to identify colors.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="61201">hexadecimal</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3041982">ହେକ୍ସ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2325_347934_485892"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The InfoPath design environment in which you can create or modify a form template.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="347934">design mode</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="485892">ଡିଜାଇନ୍ ମୋଡ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2328_21412_2572602"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To associate two pieces of information with one another.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="21412">bind</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2572602">ବାଇଣ୍ଡ୍ କରିବା</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2328_21412_484110"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To associate two pieces of information with one another.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="21412">bind</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="484110">ବନ୍ଧନ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="23319_1072508_2433751"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The XML-based vector image format for two-dimensional graphics that supports interactivity and animation and that maintains an image's appearance regardless of screen size or print size.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1072508">Scalable Vector Graphics</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2433751">SVG</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="23319_1072509_2433751"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The XML-based vector image format for two-dimensional graphics that supports interactivity and animation and that maintains an image's appearance regardless of screen size or print size.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1072509">SVG</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2433751">SVG</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2333_146857_1259007"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Row or column labels that are printed at the top of or on the left side of every page on a printed worksheet.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="146857">print titles</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259007">ମୁଦ୍ରଣ ଟାଇଟେଲସ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="23331_1073321_1259402"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A slide show mode that displays content in a manageable window that can be resized and features navigation buttons. This mode is optimized for reviewing presentations, allowing users to get the full experience, complete with animations and media, while performing other tasks, such as taking notes.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1073321">Reading View</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259402">ପଠନ ଦର୍ଶନ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="23333_1087526_1259403"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that allows users to easily add links to content within other content (e.g. pages, sections, section groups) and provides quick navigation through these links. The feature operates in the same manner that links work in wikis.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1087526">linking</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259403">ସଂଯୋଗିତ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="23334_1073349_1259404"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that highlights new or changed content in a shared notebook that the user has not yet read.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1073349">Unread Changes</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259404">ଅପଠିତ ପରିବର୍ତ୍ତନ ସମୂହ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="23335_1073356_1426241"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A high-level linear representation of a project schedule that can be easily formatted, annotated, and copied and pasted from Project into other Office applications.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1073356">timeline</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1426241">ଟାଇମଲାଇନ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="23336_1073640_1259405"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that identifies the author of unread new or changed content in a shared notebook.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1073640">Author Marks</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259405">କର୍ତ୍ତୃତ୍ୱ ଚିହ୍ନ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="23336_1073640_1346409"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that identifies the author of unread new or changed content in a shared notebook.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1073640">Author Marks</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1346409">ଗ୍ରନ୍ଥକର୍ତ୍ତା ଚିହ୍ନ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="23347_1074772_1426242"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A task pane that helps form designers to build and manage custom business rules for use in their forms.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1074772">Rules Manager</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1426242">ନୀତି ପରିଚାଳକ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="23348_1074773_1426243"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A pre-defined table style that allows users to change the look and feel of a form.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1074773">layout style</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1426243">ଲେଆଉଟ୍ ଶୈଳୀ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="23349_1074775_1426244"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that allows form designers to select from a gallery of pre-built rules to make their forms dynamic.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1074775">Quick Rules</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1426244">କୁଇକ୍ ନୀତିସମୂହ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="23351_1074778_1426245"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A pre-defined layout that users can select for their InfoPath form sections. Options include single column, two-column, three-column, and four-column layouts.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1074778">section layout</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1426245">section layout</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="23352_1216614_1426246"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An environment in the InfoPath client that enables users to fill out forms (as opposed to designing them). It must be used if the forms to be filled out are not browser-compatible.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1216614">InfoPath Filler</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1426246">Infopath Filler</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="23352_1216691_1426246"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An environment in the InfoPath client that enables users to fill out forms (as opposed to designing them). It must be used if the forms to be filled out are not browser-compatible.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1216691">Microsoft InfoPath Filler</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1426246">Infopath Filler</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="23361_1074891_2072589"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The combination of hardware (touchscreen or touchpad) and software elements that provides a way to control programs by touching multiple points on the screen simultaneously.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1074891">multi-touch</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2072589">ଏକାଧିକ-ସ୍ପର୍ଶ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="234_237832_1426130"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An object created using drawing tools or commands.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="237832">shape</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1426130">ଆକୃତି</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2342_138389_484897"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The entire chart and all its elements.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="138389">chart area</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="484897">ଚାର୍ଟ କ୍ଷେତ୍ର</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2344_21520_484111"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The set of essential software routines that test computer hardware at startup, start the operating system, and support the transfer of information between hardware devices. The BIOS is stored in read-only memory (ROM) so that it can be run when the computer is turned on. Although critical to performance, the BIOS is usually invisible to computer users.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="21520">BIOS</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="484111">BIOS</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2344_21520_484112"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The set of essential software routines that test computer hardware at startup, start the operating system, and support the transfer of information between hardware devices. The BIOS is stored in read-only memory (ROM) so that it can be run when the computer is turned on. Although critical to performance, the BIOS is usually invisible to computer users.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="21520">BIOS</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="484112">ମୌଳିକ ଇନପୁଟ୍ / ଆଉଟପୁଟ୍ ସିଷ୍ଟମ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2344_21521_484111"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The set of essential software routines that test computer hardware at startup, start the operating system, and support the transfer of information between hardware devices. The BIOS is stored in read-only memory (ROM) so that it can be run when the computer is turned on. Although critical to performance, the BIOS is usually invisible to computer users.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="21521">basic input/output system</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="484111">BIOS</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2344_21521_484112"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The set of essential software routines that test computer hardware at startup, start the operating system, and support the transfer of information between hardware devices. The BIOS is stored in read-only memory (ROM) so that it can be run when the computer is turned on. Although critical to performance, the BIOS is usually invisible to computer users.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="21521">basic input/output system</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="484112">ମୌଳିକ ଇନପୁଟ୍ / ଆଉଟପୁଟ୍ ସିଷ୍ଟମ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2346_15363_2738670"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To link one entity to another for a specific purpose.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="15363">assign</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2738670">ନ୍ୟସ୍ତ କରିବା</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="23462_1082215_1259406"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The street address or geographical coordinates of a user, and (by way of extensions) of the user’s computer or devices.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1082215">location</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammati