alNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3085777">Microsoft Defender Device Guard</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="40082_2795844_2329549"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The combination of enterprise-related hardware and software security features that, when configured together, will lock a device down so that it can only run trusted applications.​​​</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2795844">Microsoft Defender Device Guard</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2329549">Device Guard</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="40082_2795844_3085777"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The combination of enterprise-related hardware and software security features that, when configured together, will lock a device down so that it can only run trusted applications.​​​</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2795844">Microsoft Defender Device Guard</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3085777">Microsoft Defender Device Guard</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelecte