y. It tracks a precise position in space, allowing for fine-grained interaction with digital objects. When using a Windows Mixed Reality immersive headset, the motion controller is the primary way to take action.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2524057">motion controller</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2575216">Windows Mixed Reality ମୋସନ୍ କଣ୍ଟ୍ରୋଲର୍‍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44823_2531456_2575213"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A hardware accessory that allows you to take action in mixed reality. It tracks a precise position in space, allowing for fine-grained interaction with digital objects. When using a Windows Mixed Reality immersive headset, the motion controller is the primary way to take action.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2531456">Windows Mixed Reality motion controller</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2575213">ମୋସନ୍ କଣ୍ଟ୍ରୋଲର୍‍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44823_2531456_2575216"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A hardware accessory that allows you to take action in mixed reality. It tracks a precise position in space, allowing for fine-grained interaction with digital objects. When using a Windows Mixed Reality immersive headset, the motion controller is the primary way to take action.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2531456">Windows Mixed Reality motion controller</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2575216">Windows Mixed Reality ମୋସନ୍ କଣ୍ଟ୍ରୋଲର୍‍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44824_2524653_2528368"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Windows 10 update announced at Build 2017 and being released in the Sept-Nov 2017 timeframe.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2524653">Windows 10 Fall Creators Update</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2528368">Windows 10 Fall Creators Update</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44825_2524668_2528224"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature in Windows Defender Security Center that monitors your device and provides you with information and recommendations in a Health report to address common issues with your storage capacity, device drivers, battery life, or Windows Update.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2524668">Health Advisor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2528224">ହେଲ୍ଥ ପରାମର୍ଶଦାତା</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44826_2524671_2528222"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature in Windows Defender Security Center that helps you refresh your device by reinstalling and updating Windows — for example, if your device has performance issues or you have too many unnecessary apps.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2524671">Fresh Start</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2528222">ନୂତନ ଆରମ୍ଭ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44827_2524676_2528359"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The pre-release version of Microsoft Remote Desktop app.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2524676">Microsoft Remote Desktop Preview</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2528359">Microsoft ରିମୋଟ ଡେସ୍କଟପ୍‍ ପୂର୍ବାଲୋକନ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44827_2524676_2611519"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The pre-release version of Microsoft Remote Desktop app.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2524676">Microsoft Remote Desktop Preview</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2611519">ରିମୋଟ ଡେସ୍କଟପ୍‍ ପୂର୍ବାଲୋକନ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44827_2609623_2528359"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The pre-release version of Microsoft Remote Desktop app.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2609623">Remote Desktop Preview</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2528359">Microsoft ରିମୋଟ ଡେସ୍କଟପ୍‍ ପୂର୍ବାଲୋକନ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44827_2609623_2611519"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The pre-release version of Microsoft Remote Desktop app.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2609623">Remote Desktop Preview</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2611519">ରିମୋଟ ଡେସ୍କଟପ୍‍ ପୂର୍ବାଲୋକନ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44828_2524681_2528221"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The period of time when users are required to schedule a restart.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2524681">Engaged restart</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2528221">କାର୍ଯ୍ୟରତ ପୁନରାରମ୍ଭ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44829_2524692_2528370"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A system service that enables spatial perception, spatial input, and holographic rendering.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2524692">Windows Perception Service</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2528370">Windows ଅନୁଭୁତି ସେବା</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="4483_55751_484390"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A structured document or template with spaces reserved for entering information and often containing special coding (e.g. to trigger data processing).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="55751">form</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="484390">ଫର୍ମ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44832_2524734_2659322"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft interactive livestreaming platform for gaming communities.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2524734">Mixer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2659322">Mixer</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44842_2524849_2529562"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A presentation of visual elements in an image, especially the placement of the subject in relation to other objects.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2524849">frame</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2529562">ଫ୍ରେମ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44843_2524926_2528360"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A head-mounted display (HMD) that displays mixed reality experiences. Used inclusively to denote both Microsoft HoloLens and OEM devices, whether they blend virtual content within the physical world (holographic headsets), or display virtual content with a degree (big or small) of environmental awareness (immersive headsets)​. Plus, these headsets can either be self-contained (like Microsoft HoloLens - the whole computing power is contained into the headset) or PC-connected (the computing power comes from the PC and the headset cannot work without that associated PC).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2524926">mixed reality headset</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2528360">ମିଶ୍ରିତ ବାସ୍ତବିକତା ହେଡସେଟ୍‍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44843_2524926_2575211"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A head-mounted display (HMD) that displays mixed reality experiences. Used inclusively to denote both Microsoft HoloLens and OEM devices, whether they blend virtual content within the physical world (holographic headsets), or display virtual content with a degree (big or small) of environmental awareness (immersive headsets)​. Plus, these headsets can either be self-contained (like Microsoft HoloLens - the whole computing power is contained into the headset) or PC-connected (the computing power comes from the PC and the headset cannot work without that associated PC).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2524926">mixed reality headset</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2575211">ହେଡସେଟ୍‍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44843_2526431_2528360"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A head-mounted display (HMD) that displays mixed reality experiences. Used inclusively to denote both Microsoft HoloLens and OEM devices, whether they blend virtual content within the physical world (holographic headsets), or display virtual content with a degree (big or small) of environmental awareness (immersive headsets)​. Plus, these headsets can either be self-contained (like Microsoft HoloLens - the whole computing power is contained into the headset) or PC-connected (the computing power comes from the PC and the headset cannot work without that associated PC).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2526431">headset</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2528360">ମିଶ୍ରିତ ବାସ୍ତବିକତା ହେଡସେଟ୍‍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44843_2526431_2575211"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A head-mounted display (HMD) that displays mixed reality experiences. Used inclusively to denote both Microsoft HoloLens and OEM devices, whether they blend virtual content within the physical world (holographic headsets), or display virtual content with a degree (big or small) of environmental awareness (immersive headsets)​. Plus, these headsets can either be self-contained (like Microsoft HoloLens - the whole computing power is contained into the headset) or PC-connected (the computing power comes from the PC and the headset cannot work without that associated PC).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2526431">headset</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2575211">ହେଡସେଟ୍‍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44844_2524930_2528226"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A head-mounted display (HMD) that displays virtual content only and with a degree (big or small) of environmental awareness. This is a subset of "mixed reality headset."​ This is to be looked at in contrast with "holographic headsets".</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2524930">immersive headset</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2528226">ସଲଗ୍ନ ହେଡସେଟ୍‍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44845_2524937_2528364"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of moving from a lower version of a system to a higher version. A configuration shift where the user becomes able to change default settings which were locked before the shift.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2524937">switch</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2528364">ପରିବର୍ତ୍ତନ କରିବା</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44846_2524939_2528366"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To move from a lower version of a system to a higher one, or to shift system configuration in order to change default settings locked before the shift.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2524939">switch</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2528366">ପରିବର୍ତ୍ତନ କରିବା</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44861_2528507_2529563"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To arrange visual elements in an image, especially the subject.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2528507">frame</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2529563">ଫ୍ରେମ୍ କରନ୍ତୁ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44863_2529677_2530286"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft marketing campaign that emphasizes seamless use of Microsoft applications across all devices because users have just one account no matter what device they are using.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2529677">One Microsoft</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2530286">One Microsoft</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44869_2530865_2531697"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A state of an application when no documents or content is open.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2530865">zero state</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2531697">ଶୂନ୍ୟ ସ୍ଥିତି</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="4487_15671_484068"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The * character. Indicates multiplication in programming languages and also serves as a wildcard character representing one or more characters.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="15671">asterisk</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="484068">ତାରାଙ୍କିତ-ଚିହ୍ନ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singula