OfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="754_113830_484739"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A font effect in which lowercase text appears as capital letters in a reduced font size.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="113830">small caps</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="484739">ଛୋଟ-ବଡ଼ ଅକ୍ଷର</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="756_106608_1426132"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An on-screen scale marked off in inches or other units of measure and used to show line widths, tab settings, paragraph indents, and so on.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="106608">ruler</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1426132">ରୁଲର୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7561_306402_485563"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A filter effect in Windows Movie Maker.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="306402">Rotate 180</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="485563">ଆବର୍ତ୍ତ 180</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7566_184262_485116"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A delay that occurs while data is processed or delivered.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="184262">latency</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="485116">ସୁପ୍ତ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7570_140476_1259081"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The .pst data file used as the main delivery location for your email messages.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="140476">default data file</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259081">ଡିଫଲ୍ଟ ଡ଼ାଟା ଫାଇଲ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7571_170485_485073"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">One of a collection of drivers that responds to the same IRPs. Layered driver describes the highest-level and lowest-level drivers in a chain of layered drivers that process the same IRPs, along with all intermediate drivers in the chain.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="170485">layered driver</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="485073">ସ୍ତରୀଯ ଡ୍ରାଇଭର୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7581_237287_1881297"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that allows creation of mathematical formulas in documents, including the insertion of mathematical symbols inside designated "math zones" which perform automatic formatting to convert fractions, etc.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="237287">Equation Builder</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1881297">ସମୀକରଣ ନିର୍ମାତା</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7584_130154_1259978"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A portion of unique computer code contained in a virus. Antivirus programs search for known virus signatures to identify infected programs and files.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="130154">virus signature</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259978">ଭାଇରସ୍ ସ୍ୱାକ୍ଷର</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7590_375744_1957417"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that lets a Microsoft Outlook user who has a Microsoft Exchange email account work offline, either by choice or due to a connection problem. A copy of the user's mailbox is stored on their computer and is frequently updated from the mail server. Any changes that are made while a connection to the server is not available are synchronized automatically when a connection becomes available.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="375744">Cached Exchange Mode</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1957417">କ୍ୟାଚ୍ ହୋଇଥିବା Exchange ମୋଡ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7593_147682_1881202"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In a formula, the address of a cell based on the relative position of the cell that contains the formula and the cell referred to. If you copy the formula, the reference automatically adjusts.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="147682">relative reference</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1881202">ସମ୍ପର୍କ ଅନୁସରଣ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7593_147682_1881331"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In a formula, the address of a cell based on the relative position of the cell that contains the formula and the cell referred to. If you copy the formula, the reference automatically adjusts.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="147682">relative reference</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1881331">ସମ୍ପର୍କ ସେଲ୍ ଅନୁସରଣ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7593_461709_1881202"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In a formula, the address of a cell based on the relative position of the cell that contains the formula and the cell referred to. If you copy the formula, the reference automatically adjusts.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="461709">relative cell reference</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1881202">ସମ୍ପର୍କ ଅନୁସରଣ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7593_461709_1881331"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In a formula, the address of a cell based on the relative position of the cell that contains the formula and the cell referred to. If you copy the formula, the reference automatically adjusts.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="461709">relative cell reference</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1881331">ସମ୍ପର୍କ ସେଲ୍ ଅନୁସରଣ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="76_39968_1259788"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A method of protecting the rights of an originator of a creative work, such as a text, a piece of music, a painting, or a computer program, through law.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="39968">copyright</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1259788">ସତ୍ତ୍ୱାଧିକାର</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7603_148245_1881206"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The visual representation of a script on a Web page that you open in a Microsoft Office program.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="148245">script anchor</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1881206">ସ୍କ୍ରିପ୍ଟ୍ ଏଙ୍କର୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7604_137569_1881130"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In an organization chart, a shape that is placed below and connected to any other shape with an elbow connector. This shape is placed above any additional subordinate shapes for the particular superior shape it is attached to.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="137569">assistant shape</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1881130">ସହାୟକ ଆକୃତି</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7604_1509002_1881130"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In an organization chart, a shape that is placed below and connected to any other shape with an elbow connector. This shape is placed above any additional subordinate shapes for the particular superior shape it is attached to.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1509002">assistant box</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1881130">ସହାୟକ ଆକୃତି</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7612_47524_1346340"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In windowing environments, such as the Apple Macintosh and Microsoft Windows, an on-screen window (enclosed work area) in which the user can create, view, or work on a document.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="47524">document window</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1346340">ଡକ୍ୟୁମେଣ୍ଟ ଓ୍ୱିଣ୍ଡୋ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7621_1275092_1566698"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A privacy relationship setting that allows a small amount of information to be viewed, typically for nonfederated contacts.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1275092">External Contacts</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1566698">ସର୍ବସାଧାରଣ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7621_418565_1566698"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A privacy relationship setting that allows a small amount of information to be viewed, typically for nonfederated contacts.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="418565">Public</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1566698">ସର୍ବସାଧାରଣ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7628_144937_1881183"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that allows multiple design templates to be applied to a single presentation.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="144937">multiple masters</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1881183">ଏକାଧିକ ମାଷ୍ଟର୍‌ଗଣ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7631_134267_484863"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In a spreadsheet program, a file containing a number of related worksheets.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="134267">workbook</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="484863">ଶ୍ରମପୁସ୍ତିକା</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7638_398504_2818665"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A stored record of the audio and video components of a meeting or session.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="398504">recording</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2818665">ରେକର୍ଡିଂ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7641_50797_484358"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To programmatically disguise content to hide its substance.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="50797">encrypt</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="484358">ଏନକ୍ରିପ୍ଟ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7641_764958_484358"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To programmatically disguise content to hide its substance.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="764958">encipher</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="484358">ଏନକ୍ରିପ୍ଟ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">Neuter</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7642_217268_1881083"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A fixed-size result that is obtained by applying a one-way mathematical function (sometimes called a hash algorithm) to an arbitrary amount of data. If there is a change in the input data, the hash changes. The hash can be used in many operations, including authentication and digital signing.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="217268">hash code</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1881083">ହାସ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7642_2479571_1881083"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A fixed-size result that is obtained by applying a one-way mathematical function (sometimes called a hash algorithm) to an arbitrary amount of data. If there is a change in the input data, the hash changes. The hash can be used in many operations, including authentication and digital signing.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2479571">digest</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1881083">ହାସ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7642_60536_1881083"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A fixed-size result that is obtained by applying a one-way mathematical function (sometimes called a hash algorithm) to an arbitrary amount of data. If there is a change in the input data, the hash changes. The hash can be used in many operations, including authentication and digital signing.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="60536">hash</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="or-IN"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1881083">ହାସ୍</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">IND</termNote><te